# Who has to review a pull request before it can merge. GitHub reads this file
# from the branch the pull request merges into, and for each file the last
# pattern below that matches it decides its owner. It blocks a merge only once
# the ruleset on main turns on "Require review from Code Owners", and only for
# an owner with write access to the repository.

# Everything: AGENTS.md and the other rules, the scripts and the checks, the
# workflow, the shared tokens, the demo, the README in tokens/brands/ and this
# file.
*                         @ahmedamr-r

# The brand files have no owner, so a pull request that changes nothing else
# merges without that review once npm run check passes.
/tokens/brands/*.json

# A file in tokens/brands/ whose name starts with an underscore is not a brand.
# _template.json is one, and it decides what every brand may set.
/tokens/brands/_*.json    @ahmedamr-r
